  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting human rights, peace and democracy in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TAPOL (which means political prisoner in Indonesian) is a veteran human rights organisation originally set up in 1973 specifically to campaign for the tens of thousands of political prisoners who were then being held in Indonesia.  Over time TAPOL&#x2019;s mandate expanded to cover campaigning for human rights in general in Indonesia and East Timor.  Since East Timor gained its independence, TAPOL&#x2019;s involvement has gradually been phased down to focus primarily on Indonesia.  In 2007, in response to the democratic changes taking place in Indonesia, TAPOL&#x2019;s mandate changed again to cover promotion of peace, and support to the Indonesian people in their progress towards democracy, with a special focus at present on Papua.</narrative>
  </description>
